  "convention": "edge_mv = fitted resolution-smeared step centre (PSS) or bump centre (WAL/LIQ), the same convention as 22_y88_edges.py so the 07-17 and 07-28 campaigns compare directly. edge_mv_halfheight is the model-independent cross-check. The step model carries a sloped continuum under the edge: the 1836 keV Compton continuum runs through the 699 keVee edge, and Y-88's two gammas are a CASCADE, so a source on the bar produces true-coincidence summing that adds counts above every single-gamma edge \u2014 which is why the 1612 keVee edge is marked secondary and the clean single-gamma Cs-137 edge is the better low-energy anchor. Background = same channel summed over the runs with no source on that arm, scaled by trigger count. Primary fit is on the pileup-vetoed spectrum; pileup_shift_mv = (all hits) - (veto). Bootstrap {'PSS': 120, 'WAL': 40, 'LIQ': 40} Poisson resamples of signal AND background, seed 224588; error floored at half a bin (0.1 mV).",
